From d98615290c7676a9a30b5a4255e9ae3fe45a0579 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:13:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 078/144] hydra: MaterialX closures - mix, add, multiply,
 volume, layer, conductor

The families typed by their suffix went through the prefix table: `mix_bsdf`
fell on the color mix, `add_edf` on scalar math, and the closure connection fell
with a warning. They are now sorted before the table, by the nodedef suffix,
weight C/F/V removed: mix and add to mix_closure and add_closure (fg on
Closure2, as for colors), multiply to a mix against nothing whose factor is the
weight; for displacementshader, a vector in Cycles, mix_vector, vector_math and
a vector passthrough.

`volume` was missing: no MaterialX volume network could reach the terminal, no
matter its VDF. It is a sum of closures, as `surface` is a mix. `layer` was a
fifty-fifty that halved the base; it becomes a mix weighted by a Fresnel (blend
0.333, i.e. an IOR of 1.5), right for a dielectric layer on a base,
approximate for the rest. `conductor_bsdf` lost its complex index and rendered
white: it goes to metallic_bsdf as a physical conductor, ior and extinction
passed through, MaterialX's default gold.

When an output's name is not found, the first output of the same class as the
input is taken - closure, triplet or scalar - at connections as at terminals: a
surfaceshader arrives as `out` and lands on a principled whose closure is called
BSDF, a glTF image as `outcolor` on a vector helper. `dielectric_bsdf` takes
`tint` and the thin film.

Measured: five closure cases on the MaterialX bench, all exact (mix, add,
multiply and mix of surfaces to within 2 %, layer not black); mtlx_inputs goes
from 511 to 528 nodedefs without loss, 0 outputs not found, 0 missing nodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
